WEBVTT

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.721
Let me be frank.

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.724
It would be impossible
with Yukina's current marks.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:32.759
What do you mean?

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:36.530
You can only use the word "impossible"
after trying every possibility.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.398
So, have you tried everything?

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:43.403
At the very least, she will have
to raise her standard score by 30.

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:44.871
To put it simply,

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:48.508
she'll need to overtake
half a million people in 18 months.

00:01:48.742 --> 00:01:50.277
Do you think that's possible?

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:51.545
She says she wants to go.

00:01:51.612 --> 00:01:53.880
Are you just going
to stomp on her dreams?

00:01:54.181 --> 00:01:55.549
It's barely a pipe dream.

00:01:55.649 --> 00:01:57.818
It's merely wishful thinking
at this point.

00:01:58.185 --> 00:01:59.486
She can do it if she tries.

00:01:59.553 --> 00:02:02.289
Isn't it your job to tell her to try?

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.391
It's my responsibility as a teacher

00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:08.662
to have my students face reality,
and advise them on attainable goals.

00:02:08.829 --> 00:02:11.898
Adversity helps children grow.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:15.202
This is not adversity. It's reckless.

00:02:15.369 --> 00:02:20.207
Her current marks are a direct result
of her lack of talent and effort.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:24.645
Madam, please, don't assume your daughter
is the same as you were.

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.380
Every person is different.

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:31.818
I look forward to your future progress.

00:02:32.419 --> 00:02:33.854
Mother.

00:02:37.391 --> 00:02:38.892
I'm sorry, sensei.

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.228
Shirahane...

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.830
Mars isn't exactly a career choice.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:48.268
You're right.
It's a destination, isn't it?

00:02:48.335 --> 00:02:49.903
That's not my point.

00:02:50.504 --> 00:02:55.675
Besides, the Mars migration project isn't
likely to happen at this point.

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:57.644
Wait, is that yours?

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.217
Yo.

00:03:04.718 --> 00:03:06.553
Mika, which way did my mom go?

00:03:08.255 --> 00:03:08.922
Up?

00:03:09.423 --> 00:03:12.359
-What's wrong?
-Mom forgot her phone.

00:03:12.426 --> 00:03:14.561
Whoa, awesome. Is it for the U.N.?

00:03:14.628 --> 00:03:16.430
That's so cool.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.801
Mother, you forgot this!

00:03:21.468 --> 00:03:22.569
Mom!

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:26.373
Yukina, there aren't any Martians, okay?

00:03:38.719 --> 00:03:40.420
She's so cool.

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:43.657
Your mom is so cool.

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.960
There's nothing motherly about her.

00:03:47.561 --> 00:03:49.863
My mom's just a plain old lady.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:53.266
Compared to that,
your mom's the head of the laboratory.

00:03:56.303 --> 00:03:57.871
So, how did career counseling go?

00:03:58.338 --> 00:03:59.339
What'd you write?

00:04:00.307 --> 00:04:01.007
Mars.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:03.276
Is that the hot one?

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:04.611
The cold one.

00:04:04.945 --> 00:04:06.646
But I can't believe it.

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.316
My mom didn't object at all.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.818
Take your future more seriously.

00:04:12.953 --> 00:04:14.554
But why Mars?

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:18.291
Because I thought it'd be cool
to see the canals on Mars.

00:04:19.493 --> 00:04:20.761
Do they really exist?

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:21.695
They don't?

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.864
I thought they said they didn't.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:25.532
No way.

00:04:25.699 --> 00:04:27.601
They're definitely hiding something.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:30.871
You really love crap like that.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.309
Seeing river terraces on Mars
would be cool, too.

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:37.878
I don't know what that means.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:40.447
And isn't that your mom's?

00:04:40.814 --> 00:04:41.681
Oh, I forgot.

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:46.019
It's so like your mom
to forget something that important.

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:48.822
But now you've gotta take it to her.

00:04:49.456 --> 00:04:51.658
What? No way. I don't wanna go.

00:04:51.825 --> 00:04:53.293
Quit your whining.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:54.528
Follow me.

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:55.929
Let's go.

00:04:57.798 --> 00:04:58.932
Hey.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.469
Come on, hurry up.

00:05:07.641 --> 00:05:09.576
Oh, hey there, Sophie.

00:05:09.643 --> 00:05:11.611
Did you have a guidance meeting, too?

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:13.079
Hello.

00:05:13.647 --> 00:05:16.483
No, because I do not need one.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:19.052
Oh, that's right. You're still young.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:21.521
I have already chosen my career.

00:05:21.588 --> 00:05:25.358
I simply need to hone what I am doing now.
What about you, Yukina?

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.861
-I...
-She said Mars.

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:29.930
Mars? The red planet?

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:31.898
That's right, where the Martians are.

00:05:32.566 --> 00:05:35.902
Perhaps you should be limiting your jokes
to less essential matters.

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:37.337
I'm sorry.

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:39.472
Are you off to work, Sophie?

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:41.741
Yes. So, farewell.

00:05:44.778 --> 00:05:46.746
-Bye.
-Bye.

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:50.483
She is so amazing.
I mean, she even skipped a grade.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:53.887
And she works at the U.N. laboratory.

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:56.790
She's nothing like us.

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:59.459
Oh, I know.
I'll have her take this with her.

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:03.730
Sophie, take this with you!

00:06:04.431 --> 00:06:05.131
Miss.

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:07.867
Your friend is running after us.

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:10.136
-Please, don't slow down.
-Yes, miss.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:22.816
We're getting on!

00:06:45.105 --> 00:06:47.707
Look how the water level's
changed its flow.

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:50.644
Don't you ever get tired of looking at it?

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:51.978
No way.

00:06:52.512 --> 00:06:53.680
That right?

00:06:57.951 --> 00:06:59.919
Hey, hold on!

00:07:05.592 --> 00:07:08.495
It's the dam!

00:07:09.529 --> 00:07:11.665
Why's it always so awesome?

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:12.699
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:12.866 --> 00:07:15.201
You can look at it as much as you want
on our way home.

00:07:28.715 --> 00:07:31.051
Whoa, they're huge.

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:34.020
I forgot, did your mom make those?

00:07:34.087 --> 00:07:35.522
Seems like she did.

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:48.001
Why do you hate coming here?

00:07:48.702 --> 00:07:50.637
I don't like it that much.

00:07:56.176 --> 00:07:57.510
Being treated like that.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:02.482
You're the chief's daughter, after all.

00:08:02.549 --> 00:08:04.784
It makes me so nervous.

00:08:04.851 --> 00:08:06.252
Everybody looking at me.

00:08:06.987 --> 00:08:09.789
Hey, Mika.
What did you write for your career?

00:08:09.956 --> 00:08:11.725
Probably getting a job.

00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:12.859
Get a job where?

00:08:13.159 --> 00:08:14.094
Who knows?

00:08:14.594 --> 00:08:20.033
Anywhere that'd hire an idiot
without talent, work ethic, or brains.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.736
It'd be pretty tough with your marks.

00:08:23.136 --> 00:08:27.540
My family always says
that great talent matures later.

00:08:27.607 --> 00:08:31.945
So, if I get hired,
I know I'd do a good job.

00:08:32.045 --> 00:08:35.248
Watching you really makes me want
to try harder.

00:08:36.883 --> 00:08:39.285
I feel like you're making fun of me.

00:08:39.552 --> 00:08:40.920
Not at all.

00:08:41.521 --> 00:08:44.124
Well, I'm going to go surprise my dad.

00:08:44.524 --> 00:08:46.926
-He works in the cafeteria, right?
-Yeah, he's a chef.

00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:48.928
I'm sure he won't be busy right now.

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:49.963
Meet back at four?

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:52.232
Sounds good. See you later.

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:53.666
Bye.

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:01.875
Honestly.

00:09:02.042 --> 00:09:04.878
Why didn't you just hand it to me
at school?

00:09:05.311 --> 00:09:06.646
You're always like this.

00:09:06.713 --> 00:09:09.249
You don't listen to anybody else.

00:09:10.717 --> 00:09:11.684
Here.

00:09:11.851 --> 00:09:13.053
Thanks.

00:09:13.319 --> 00:09:17.123
Anyway, you'll need to work harder
if you want to go to Mars.

00:09:17.624 --> 00:09:19.859
I don't think working hard will be enough.

00:09:19.926 --> 00:09:23.096
Don't worry,
you're my daughter, after all.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.065
Stop that.

00:09:25.698 --> 00:09:29.736
Oh, but you'll have to wait until
Koharu grows up before you leave for Mars.

00:09:29.903 --> 00:09:32.605
Would it kill you to raise her yourself?

00:09:32.672 --> 00:09:35.008
Well, I raised you, didn't I?

00:09:35.075 --> 00:09:37.877
Uncle's the one who raised me.

00:09:38.678 --> 00:09:41.848
Children never understand
what their parents go through.

00:09:42.248 --> 00:09:45.251
How about you try a little harder
and make your teacher eat his words?

00:09:51.891 --> 00:09:54.594
You only act like a mother
when it's convenient.

00:09:56.796 --> 00:09:58.331
What am I going to do?

00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:03.069
DEFENSE MINISTRY

00:10:05.071 --> 00:10:06.973
It's not a ballistic missile?

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.342
It's not the size of a missile.

00:10:09.709 --> 00:10:11.177
We believe it's a meteorite.

00:10:11.945 --> 00:10:14.013
Trajectory's angle of inclination
is 98 degrees.

00:10:14.614 --> 00:10:16.182
Groundspeed is two kilometers per second.

00:10:16.316 --> 00:10:19.219
Two kilometers?
That seems slow for a meteorite.

00:10:19.385 --> 00:10:21.154
Object 1 has entered the atmosphere.

00:10:21.855 --> 00:10:23.656
We've calculated its point of impact.

00:10:25.758 --> 00:10:29.229
Several fragments are breaking off
of Object 1.

00:10:29.395 --> 00:10:32.098
-Did it break apart?
-Unable to confirm.

00:10:32.699 --> 00:10:34.901
Object 1 is slowing down.

00:10:35.268 --> 00:10:36.236
What?

00:10:38.938 --> 00:10:43.843
A Rain of Ogres from the Sky

00:10:48.848 --> 00:10:51.951
The bad ogres are going to come again.

00:10:52.986 --> 00:10:53.853
Again?

00:10:54.254 --> 00:10:55.121
That's right.

00:10:55.755 --> 00:10:57.924
From a world far, far away.

00:10:58.758 --> 00:11:01.828
They're returning to eat the humans.

00:11:02.929 --> 00:11:04.764
They're gonna eat us.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:07.867
Crap.

00:11:08.434 --> 00:11:11.271
Oh, it's still 3:30.

00:11:19.212 --> 00:11:20.113
Mr. Aramata.

00:11:21.014 --> 00:11:22.315
Oh, Yuki.

00:11:22.382 --> 00:11:23.416
Hello!

00:11:23.683 --> 00:11:25.418
Here to see Hiromi?

00:11:25.685 --> 00:11:27.053
Well, yes.

00:11:27.453 --> 00:11:31.024
I keep telling her
to go home once in a while.

00:11:31.758 --> 00:11:32.926
Who is that?

00:11:32.992 --> 00:11:35.194
That's Hiromi's daughter Yukina.

00:11:35.828 --> 00:11:38.197
I see, so, that's her.

00:11:38.798 --> 00:11:41.401
I think I've... seen that thing before.

00:11:42.468 --> 00:11:44.404
It's the Cube.

00:11:44.771 --> 00:11:45.738
I know it.

00:11:45.805 --> 00:11:49.776
It was found during the construction
of a tunnel 60 years ago.

00:11:49.842 --> 00:11:51.010
Very good.

00:11:51.077 --> 00:11:53.746
But are you sure it's okay for me
to see it?

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:55.148
No problem at all.

00:11:55.481 --> 00:11:58.184
It's an Artifact
that's already been made public.

00:11:58.351 --> 00:12:00.887
Not that we've found anything out
about it.

00:12:01.054 --> 00:12:04.390
I guess the giant below is better
compared to this.

00:12:04.924 --> 00:12:05.858
Giant?

00:12:06.025 --> 00:12:10.263
<i>It's another Artifact that hasn't really
<i>been made public.</i></i>

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:13.433
<i>It's also the reason
<i>this laboratory was built here.</i></i>

00:12:14.434 --> 00:12:16.836
What reason is that?

00:12:17.003 --> 00:12:18.771
It's because we can't move it.

00:12:19.005 --> 00:12:22.809
But I'd say it's more of an ogre
than a giant.

00:12:23.309 --> 00:12:25.178
Ogre?

00:12:26.179 --> 00:12:28.147
Professor Takehito Shirahane.

00:12:28.514 --> 00:12:32.318
Your father was studying
the local folklore around here, wasn't he?

00:12:32.952 --> 00:12:34.153
Yes.

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.789
Did your father not mention anything?

00:12:37.023 --> 00:12:38.191
About the ogres?

00:12:38.424 --> 00:12:41.394
My father hasn't been back
since disappearing eight years ago.

00:12:43.796 --> 00:12:45.164
Oh, I see.

00:12:46.065 --> 00:12:47.266
Dumbass.

00:12:56.876 --> 00:12:57.543
What's going on?

00:13:01.447 --> 00:13:02.815
Is this...?

00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:04.517
Get back!

00:13:17.897 --> 00:13:19.265
What was that?

00:13:29.809 --> 00:13:31.144
Ground impact confirmed!

00:13:31.911 --> 00:13:34.147
Three kilometers offshore Toyama Bay.

00:13:35.048 --> 00:13:37.383
<i>Michishio,
a nearby Maritime SDF submarine,</i>

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:38.951
is heading to inspect it.

00:13:39.118 --> 00:13:40.353
What about the fragments?

00:13:40.987 --> 00:13:43.189
Crashed somewhere
between Toyama and Nagano.

00:13:43.356 --> 00:13:45.491
It's also crashed into a U.N. facility.

00:13:52.398 --> 00:13:54.167
Mr. Aramata, are you okay?

00:13:54.867 --> 00:13:56.335
Oh, my God.

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:59.272
Was it a meteorite?

00:14:00.373 --> 00:14:02.241
An actual meteorite?

00:14:22.228 --> 00:14:24.130
Hurry up!

00:14:25.064 --> 00:14:27.900
This is the United Nations
Research Laboratory.

00:14:28.301 --> 00:14:30.903
You will be fired upon for trespassing.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.472
Vacate immediately.

00:15:03.302 --> 00:15:04.604
What are those?

00:15:05.271 --> 00:15:07.673
It's dangerous.
We need to run to the basement.

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:09.075
What about you?

00:15:09.242 --> 00:15:11.344
I'm going to find your mother.

00:15:11.511 --> 00:15:13.079
I'm going back to the lab.

00:15:13.279 --> 00:15:15.314
You two need to evacuate to the basement.

00:15:30.196 --> 00:15:31.464
Prioritize extinguishing the fire.

00:15:32.031 --> 00:15:34.133
Just keep them out of the facility.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.202
You don't have to engage the large one.

00:15:37.236 --> 00:15:41.140
I will take command from here.
Do I have your permission?

00:15:41.307 --> 00:15:44.410
Of course, Major Graham.
I leave this to you.

00:15:45.711 --> 00:15:48.948
This facility will be following
emergency protocol.

00:15:49.382 --> 00:15:52.251
All orders will be sent
from the Garrison HQ.

00:15:52.418 --> 00:15:55.254
Alpha Squad, prevent enemy infiltration
from the west gate.

00:15:55.421 --> 00:15:56.989
What's your current status?

00:15:57.056 --> 00:15:58.958
I don't want to admit it.

00:15:59.125 --> 00:16:01.327
But does that mean he was right?

00:16:01.494 --> 00:16:02.628
It looks like it.

00:16:03.062 --> 00:16:05.631
But I wish they would've waited until
after I retired.

00:16:06.332 --> 00:16:08.601
Major, incoming from
GAUS 1's Captain Borden.

00:16:08.968 --> 00:16:10.069
<i>Major.</i>

00:16:10.136 --> 00:16:12.538
<i>What's all this crap we have?</i>

00:16:12.972 --> 00:16:15.107
<i>Why keep it around
<i>if we're not gonna use it?</i></i>

00:16:16.375 --> 00:16:18.010
Can it be deployed?

00:16:18.211 --> 00:16:21.080
It's not in peak condition,
but I guarantee it'll move.

00:16:21.481 --> 00:16:23.716
It has a one-hour operation limit.

00:16:24.217 --> 00:16:27.053
But the consumption rate
during real combat is unknown.

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:30.423
Have you finished testing the mass driver?

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:33.025
We haven't actually fired it yet.

00:16:33.092 --> 00:16:34.193
Do you want to use it?

00:16:34.494 --> 00:16:36.362
I don't want to open the gate.

00:16:36.562 --> 00:16:38.598
GAUS 1, GAUS 2, prepare to deploy.

00:16:38.998 --> 00:16:41.000
Launch the mass driver at minimum output.

00:16:41.167 --> 00:16:42.702
Those idiots.

00:16:43.069 --> 00:16:44.604
Hurry up and get us up there.

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:47.106
The fight's gonna be over
before we get there.

00:16:47.173 --> 00:16:49.675
Gravity stabilizer, max output.

00:16:49.742 --> 00:16:52.578
Inertia canceller calibration, check.

00:16:53.212 --> 00:16:55.448
Graviton convergence, check.

00:17:03.322 --> 00:17:06.125
Time to take the trash out.

00:18:02.782 --> 00:18:05.318
Where am I?

00:18:08.688 --> 00:18:10.590
Is it not broken?

00:18:19.732 --> 00:18:20.600
Princess.

00:18:22.234 --> 00:18:24.804
-You are safe.
-What now?

00:18:25.771 --> 00:18:26.806
I was...

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:30.643
I was mistaken...

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:33.179
Who are you?

00:18:33.646 --> 00:18:35.481
Kennosuke Tokisada Oma.

00:18:35.815 --> 00:18:37.817
Did the ogres send you?!

00:18:50.896 --> 00:18:52.798
I'll show you a good time, baby.

00:18:52.865 --> 00:18:55.201
You ain't gonna be able to walk straight.

00:19:01.907 --> 00:19:04.410
You're one fast bitch.

00:19:04.477 --> 00:19:06.212
You headless bastard!

00:19:13.586 --> 00:19:16.389
You trying to kill us, you dumb wench?!

00:19:16.789 --> 00:19:17.757
My apologies.

00:19:56.662 --> 00:19:57.663
Damn it.

00:19:57.830 --> 00:20:00.433
I'll split your head open
and take a dump in it.

00:20:20.786 --> 00:20:21.854
Nice shot.

00:20:22.822 --> 00:20:26.726
Hope you like that 120 mm up your ass.

00:20:56.455 --> 00:20:57.656
Princess...

00:21:00.326 --> 00:21:01.260
Are you unharmed?

00:21:01.761 --> 00:21:02.962
Over there.

00:21:03.028 --> 00:21:04.497
Vile hands of the ogre.

00:21:05.464 --> 00:21:07.266
What are you going to do to Yukina?

00:21:08.601 --> 00:21:09.602
Yukina?

00:21:18.611 --> 00:21:20.746
Who is this man?

00:21:21.914 --> 00:21:23.749
A stranger.

00:23:42.955 --> 00:23:48.027
<i>So, apparently GAUS is an acronym
<i>for Gravity Attenuation Upright Shell.</i></i>

00:23:48.093 --> 00:23:50.095
<i>It was built at Kurobe Laboratory.</i>
